@nsobid-9B4E43650501A4D4489B4BBFDB740F26AF3CF850

# Ganon beam mod, TotK 1.2.1 main.
# ShootControllerToggle update (0x710174694c) calls 0x7101743ea8 first: it returns true when a ray from the shooter to the beam
# origin hits anything, and then the beam body effect is killed (and re-emitted on a later frame). A Master Sword in Link's hand
# keeps tripping it, so the beam shows for a frame or two. The patch makes that call return 0 (never occluded).
@flag offset_shift 0x100

@enabled
01746984 00008052
@stop
